{
  "_comment": [
    "The one grammar of a threshold value's `value[:severity]` suffix (#3071): split at",
    "the LAST `:`, trim both halves (Go strings.TrimSpace), lower-case an ASCII suffix;",
    "no `:` is warning; a suffix outside `severities` is an unreadable value (`ok` false).",
    "`value_part` / `severity` are splitThresholdSeverity's halves, `float_ok` whether",
    "`custom_alert_disabled`: resolveOneCustomAlert reads the threshold as the opt-out.",
    "strconv.ParseFloat reads `value_part`; `severities` is config.ThresholdSeverities().",
    "⛔ Never hand-edit those columns: add a row with only `value`, then run",
    "`DA_REGEN_THRESHOLD_VALUE_MATRIX=1 go test ./pkg/config -run TestThresholdValueMatrix`",
    "in components/threshold-exporter/app, which writes them from Go.",
    "Go half: pkg/config/threshold_value_parity_test.go (the file says what Go says; the",
    "row resolvers, custom alerts and the subtree overlay agree). Python half:",
    "tests/shared/test_threshold_value_parity.py (backtest_threshold.parse_threshold_value,",
    "custom_alerts/shape.py parse_threshold and _COMPARED_SEVERITIES agree)."
  ],
